# System options of the PC kernel on top of x86_64_defconfig.
# The CPU clock stays at its top rate. x86_64_defconfig makes userspace the
# default governor, and intel_pstate and amd-pstate then start in powersave:
# the clock falls while the frame thread waits for the vertical blank, and a
# heavy core misses fields (Core i3-6100T, FinalBurn Neo, Metal Slug X: 42
# frames per second and 18 missed fields per second; 60.2 and none with
# performance). check-kernel-config.sh requires it.
CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_DEFAULT_GOV_PERFORMANCE=y
# CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_DEFAULT_GOV_USERSPACE is not set
